[199.631417, "o", "\r\u001b[2KI’ll add the Blog page with the three posts from the CV, brief research-oriented summaries, and sidebar links that connect back to the publications and contact \r\nsections.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app/my_website && cat > public/blog.html <<'EOF'\r\n<!doctype html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n<head>\r\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\r\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\r\n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Research notes by Dr. Lydia Moreno on interpretable machine learning, single-cell genomics, and graph neural networks for \r\nconnectomics.\">\r\n  <title>Blog | Lydia Moreno, Ph.D.</title>\r\n  <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"assets/favicon.svg\" type=\"image/svg+xml\">\r\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\r\n</head>\r\n<body>\r\n  <a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a>\r\n\r\n  <header class=\"site-header\">\r\n    <div class=\"container nav-wrap\">\r\n      <a class=\"brand\" href=\"index.html\" aria-label=\"Lydia Moreno — home\">\r\n        <span class=\"brand-mark\" aria-hidden=\"true\">LM</span>\r\n        <span class=\"brand-text\">\r\n          <strong>Lydia Moreno</strong>\r\n          <small>Computational Neuroscience</small>\r\n        </span>\r\n      </a>\r\n      <nav class=\"site-nav\" aria-label=\"Primary navigation\">\r\n        <a href=\"index.html\">About Me</a>\r\n        <a href=\"blog.html\" aria-current=\"page\">Blog</a>\r\n        <a href=\"publications.html\">Publications</a>\r\n      </nav>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </header>\r\n\r\n  <main id=\"main\">\r\n    <section class=\"container page-hero\" aria-labelledby=\"blog-title\">\r\n      <p class=\"eyebrow\">Notes from the lab</p>\r\n      <h1 id=\"blog-title\">Writing about models, minds, and data.</h1>\r\n      <p class=\"intro\">\r\n        Short reflections on interpretability, computational biology, and the practical\r\n        work of turning complex neural data into useful scientific insight.\r\n      </p>\r\n    </section>\r\n\r\n    <section class=\"container section-tight\" aria-label=\"Latest blog posts\">\r\n      <div class=\"blog-layout\">\r\n        <div class=\"post-list\">\r\n          <article class=\"post-card\" id=\"interpretable-deep-learning\">\r\n            <div class=\"post-meta\">\r\n              <time datetime=\"2025-03\">March 2025</time>\r\n              <span class=\"dot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\r\n              <span>Explainable AI</span>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <h2>Building Interpretable Deep Learning Models for Neuroscience</h2>\r\n            <p>\r\n              A model that predicts neural activity is only the beginning. In this note,\r\n              I reflect on treating interpretability as a design constraint: choosing\r\n              representations that can be inspected, testing feature attributions against\r\n              controlled perturbations, and reporting where a model’s explanations become\r\n              fragile.\r\n            </p>\r\n            <p class=\"post-note\">\r\n              Related thread: explainable AI methods for neural decoding and the importance\r\n              of model behavior that neuroscientists can interrogate.\r\n            </p>\r\n          </article>\r\n\r\n          <article class=\"post-card\" id=\"ml-single-cell-genomics\">\r\n            <div class=\"post-meta\">\r\n              <time datetime=\"2025-01\">January 2025</time>\r\n              <span class=\"dot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\r\n              <span>Single-cell omics</span>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <h2>Bridging Machine Learning and Single-Cell Genomics</h2>\r\n            <p>\r\n              Multi-modal single-cell data offer a remarkable view of cellular identity,\r\n              but integrate them carefully: normalization choices, batch structure, and\r\n              missing modalities all shape the biological conclusions. I outline a\r\n              practical workflow for keeping preprocessing decisions visible and for\r\n              validating clusters against independent evidence.\r\n            </p>\r\n            <p class=\"post-note\">\r\n              Related thread: scalable pipelines for single-cell genomics and spatial\r\n              transcriptomics.\r\n            </p>\r\n          </article>\r\n\r\n          <article class=\"post-card\" id=\"scaling-gnn-co"]
[199.631566, "o", "nnectomics\">\r\n            <div class=\"post-meta\">\r\n              <time datetime=\"2024-11\">November 2024</time>\r\n              <span class=\"dot\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\r\n              <span>Connectomics</span>\r\n            </div>\r\n            <h2>Scaling Graph Neural Networks for Connectomics</h2>\r\n            <p>\r\n              Connectomic graphs are large, sparse, and biologically structured. Scaling\r\n              graph learning here is not only a hardware problem; it is a question of\r\n              preserving local circuit motifs while sampling efficiently across the\r\n              reconstruction. I discuss representation choices that helped our team infer\r\n              synapse types and connectivity patterns at useful scale.\r\n            </p>\r\n            <p class=\"post-note\">\r\n              Related thread: graph neural networks for circuit analysis and the NeuroGraph\r\n              project.\r\n            </p>\r\n          </article>\r\n        </div>\r\n\r\n        <aside class=\"blog-sidebar\" aria-label=\"Blog sidebar\">\r\n          <section class=\"sidebar-card\" aria-labelledby=\"topics-title\">\r\n            <h2 id=\"topics-title\">Topics I write about</h2>\r\n            <ul class=\"tag-list\">\r\n              <li>Explainable AI</li>\r\n              <li>Neural decoding</li>\r\n              <li>Biomedical imaging</li>\r\n              <li>Single-cell omics</li>\r\n              <li>Connectomics</li>\r\n              <li>Open science</li>\r\n            </ul>\r\n          </section>\r\n\r\n          <section class=\"sidebar-card\" aria-labelledby=\"reading-title\">\r\n            <h2 id=\"reading-title\">Explore the research</h2>\r\n            <p>\r\n              Peer-reviewed work from the lab spans computational neuroscience,\r\n              neuroinformatics, and single-cell biology.\r\n            </p>\r\n            <a class=\"text-link\" href=\"publications.html\">View publications</a>\r\n          </section>\r\n\r\n          <section class=\"sidebar-card\" aria-labelledby=\"discuss-title\">\r\n            <h2 id=\"discuss-title\">Join the conversation</h2>\r\n            <p>\r\n              Have a question about a post or an idea for a collaboration?\r\n            </p>\r\n            <a class=\"text-link\" href=\"mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu\">Get in touch</a>\r\n          </section>\r\n        </aside>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </section>\r\n  </main>\r\n\r\n  <footer class=\"site-footer\">\r\n    <div class=\"container footer-inner\">\r\n      <p>© 2025 Lydia Moreno. Research profile and selected work.</p>\r\n      <div class=\"footer-links\">\r\n        <a href=\"index.html\">About Me</a>\r\n        <a href=\"blog.html\">Blog</a>\r\n        <a href=\"publications.html\">Publications</a>\r\n        <a href=\"mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu\">Contact</a>\r\n      </div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </footer>\r\n</body>\r\n</html>\r\nEOF\r\necho \"blog.html created: $(wc -l < public/blog.html) lines\"\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
